From bc6568ae266d969727cc883f7d7f876d06eafb06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Konstantin Pereiaslov <perk11@perk11.info>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 06:31:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] tci: inline TLB probe + direct helper dispatch (all TCI
 builds, not just wasm)

TCI routes every guest memory access and every helper call through
libffi's ffi_call, which emscripten implements as a JS round-trip
(ffi_call_js: argument arrays + BigInt marshalling +
getWasmTableEntry(fn).apply(), ~1.7us) - and which on native hosts
still re-marshals every argument.  The S75 firmware's busy-poll loops
are dominated by exactly these two paths.

  * tci_qemu_ld/tci_qemu_st: probe the softmmu TLB inline before
    calling the helper, mirroring the compare native TCG backends emit
    (prepare_host_addr / tlb_set_compare): on (addr[+s-a] &
    (page_mask|a_mask)) == tlb_addr the entry is valid RAM, dirty,
    watchpoint-free and cannot straddle a page, so addr+addend is the
    host address and a single load/store suffices.  Byte swapping,
    sign extension, alignment and MO_ATOM_* requirements handled;
    everything else falls back to the helpers.

  * INDEX_op_call: classify the call's libffi signature (i32/i64
    words, <= 5 args, void/u32/u64 return; pointers per host pointer
    size) and call the helper through an exactly-typed function
    pointer instead of ffi_call - a native wasm call_indirect with no
    JS involvement (a plain indirect call on native hosts).
    TCI_TAG_UNCLASSIFIED marks signatures that must keep using libffi
    (note: distinct from the valid tag of a (void)->void helper, which
    the first revision of this patch accidentally routed through
    libffi).

NOT wasm-gated; measured on native Linux TCI (S75 fullflash):
  default timing model   splash milestone   40.9 s -> 36.9 s  (-10%)
  icount2 (helper/insn)  steady rate        13.8  -> 19.9 MHz (+44%)
wasm (headless Chromium, v=2..7 window): unchanged-to-better vs an
emscripten-gated revision (interleaved runs, host noise +-6%).
Native TCG backends are untouched; removing this patch (with its
dependents) collapses wasm boot progress ~25x (isolation testing,
2026-09-09).

Assisted-by: GLM-5.3
